@using SpaceSails.Core

@* #741 · THE NOTEBOOK'S NODES — one block of the case, drawn.

   Owner's UI spec, from the chair where it happened: "title-first, collapsed by default: every note shows
   its TITLE and an expand button; the reading surface is the list of titles, not walls of text… the opened
   node houses its text as bullets… notes already CONNECTED read differently at title level from unconnected
   ones — so the collapsed list is itself a case status: which titles are still loose ends."

   It decides NOTHING. Which rows sit together, which pair carries a red edge, how many lines run off a note
   and what its title says are all read off CaseThreads.Row, which the page handed down. A component that
   re-derived any of that would be this repository's third named bug class — a drawn shape reporting one
   thing while the sim does another.

   The red line is drawn as a RAIL down the left of a block, plus a solid connector between two rows a hand
   actually threaded. Those are two different claims and they are drawn as two different marks: a rail says
   "these belong to one case", a connector says "somebody drew THIS line". A block of four hung off one hub
   cannot be a straight path, and a page that drew it as one would be lying about which pairs were
   connected. *@

@foreach (CaseThreads.Row row in Rows)
{
    string id = row.Id;
    bool open = IsOpen(id);
    bool held = IsHeld(id);

    <div class="note-node @(row.ClusterSize > 1 ? "in-case" : "") @(held ? "held" : "")">
        <button type="button"
                class="note-title @(PenInHand ? "pen" : "")"
                title="@(PenInHand
                          ? CaseThreads.PenInHandHint
                          : (open ? "Fold it again" : "Open it and read the bullets"))"
                @onclick="() => OnTitle.InvokeAsync(id)">
            <span class="note-caret">@(PenInHand ? "🖊" : open ? "▾" : "▸")</span>
            <span class="note-title-text">@row.Note.Glyph @CaseThreads.TitleOf(row.Note)</span>
            @if (row.Threads > 0)
            {
                <span class="note-threads" title="@($"{row.Threads} drawn from this one")">
                    🧵 @row.Threads
                </span>
            }
            else
            {
                <span class="note-loose">@CaseThreads.LooseEndLabel</span>
            }
        </button>

        @if (WithPlace)
        {
            @* THE CASE reading demotes the ground from a heading to a fact about the entry, because the
               ORDER there belongs to the red lines. Nothing is lost: it is the same PlaceLabel the book
               writes, and the every-ground reading still puts it up top where a walk is reconstructed. *@
            <div class="note-place">🥾 @row.Note.Place</div>
        }

        @if (open)
        {
            <ul class="note-bullets">
                @foreach (string bullet in CaseThreads.BulletsOf(row.Note))
                {
                    <li>@bullet</li>
                }
            </ul>
        }
    </div>

    @if (row.ThreadedToNext)
    {
        <div class="note-line" aria-label="a line drawn between these two"></div>
    }
}

@code {
    /// <summary>The rows to draw, in the order Core put them.</summary>
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyList<CaseThreads.Row> Rows { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>Whether the pen is out — which is what pressing a title MEANS, and nothing else.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool PenInHand { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the ground each entry came off is drawn on the node. True only in the case
    /// reading, where place is no longer the heading.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool WithPlace { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Is this node open? Asked of the page, which keys it on the HANDLE — so a node stays open
    /// across the reorder a drawn line causes, and the reading does not close under the captain's eye.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<string, bool> IsOpen { get; set; } = _ => false;

    /// <summary>Is this the title already picked up, waiting for its other end?</summary>
    [Parameter] public Func<string, bool> IsHeld { get; set; } = _ => false;

    /// <summary>A title was pressed. What that means is the page's business.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<string> OnTitle { get; set; }
}
